{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261027T224518Z-db42fd51", "ts": "2026-10-27T22:47:31Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.0-dev.2", "branch": "feature/1086-build-stamp"}, "body": {"base_commit": "eb4de60ea330e0d9cfc8e1a40665936e76b2d2ad", "base_tree": "d28058350bc526e7fcfae56e34065884436ebebd", "head_tree": "dac419b38b9e6acc874f13ae95668478af7d9197", "head_commit": "f9f0db70c375f145e72e3ea2ac1df937a5f8bdb2", "dispatch_commit": "f9f0db70c375f145e72e3ea2ac1df937a5f8bdb2", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/lib/evidence.py", "plugin/lib/stats.py", "tests/test_contribution.py", "tests/test_evidence_build_stamp.py", "tests/test_evidence_ephemeral_provenance.py", "tests/test_stats.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-build-stamp.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/kernel-v3-evidence-design.md", ".prawduct/changes/build-stamp.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/lib/evidence.py", "plugin/lib/stats.py", "tests/test_contribution.py", "tests/test_evidence_build_stamp.py", "tests/test_evidence_ephemeral_provenance.py", "tests/test_stats.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-build-stamp.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/kernel-v3-evidence-design.md", ".prawduct/changes/build-stamp.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "warning", "title": "build-stamp git status runs without GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, so a fact append can refresh (and lock) the plugin checkout's index", "recommendation": "read_plugin_build calls `git status --porcelain=v2 --branch -- .` in the plugin root with an env that only strips the repo-locating variables. Plain `git status` takes index.lock opportunistically and rewrites the index when stat info is stale. The plugin root is a developer's working checkout: prawduct-live, which every governed repo runs, or this repo under --plugin-dir. So any hook process that appends a fact can take a lock there that collides with a concurrent `git add`/`commit` in that checkout ('Unable to create index.lock: File exists'). It also bumps the index mtime, which stranded_work/git_hygiene read as a sign of life. Every other read-only status/probe in the plugin sets this deliberately (gitstate._run_git_text: 'a read must never refresh an index'; git_hygiene.py:158; stranded_work.py:220). Add `\"GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS\": \"0\"` to the env built in read_plugin_build, or pass `--no-optional-locks`. Pin it with a test that the status call's env carries it, or that the plugin checkout's index mtime is unchanged after read_plugin_build on a tree with stale stat info.", "files": ["plugin/lib/evidence.py", "tests/test_evidence_build_stamp.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "Hand-rolled process memo where functools.cache fits", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `_plugin_build` keeps a module-global `_build_memo` with an `_UNREAD` sentinel and a `# type: ignore` so that it can cache a None result. `functools.cache` on the zero-argument function does the same (None included) with no sentinel and no type ignore, and tests would call `_plugin_build.cache_clear()` in place of monkeypatching `_build_memo`. Nothing behaves wrongly today. This is an optional simplification, and no edit is required.", "files": ["plugin/lib/evidence.py", "tests/test_evidence_build_stamp.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "by_build rows do not add up to their version's numbers, and the prose says 'split'", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `aggregate_by_build`'s docstring says a version's rows \"split its numbers\". The governance-telemetry.md paragraph says each row is \"defined exactly as a version's numbers are\". That second statement is true. But sessions, scopes, rounds-per-scope medians and p90s count a unit once in every build it spans, the same way the existing version-bump rule works. So the per-build rows are not a partition that sums to the `by_version` row. A reader comparing builds could add them up and expect the version total. If you want to close this, make the docstring relational, along the lines of \"each build row is computed as a version row is, so units spanning builds count in each\". Otherwise accept the NOTE. It is prose, nothing reads it, and no edit is required.", "files": ["plugin/lib/stats.py", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner (build-stamp)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The plan records eight mid-build decisions, each with its reason. Chunk 01: dirty counts untracked-unignored files as well as modified ones (an alignment-pass miss: the plan said 'uncommitted changes' without saying which). VERSION must be tracked for a root to count as a checkout (inferred). Repo-locating GIT_* variables are stripped (inferred). One status call plus one ls-files call, fail to omit, memoised including None, with a dated cost measurement. actor.build travels in the notes transport to the product's remote, 'Flagged for the owner'. Chunk 02: --by-build adds a by_build key rather than re-keying, so REPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION stays at 2. Rows are ordered by when the store first saw them, and a non-string build counts as unstamped. contribution.py needed no change and is pinned by two tests. The one with no confirmation on record is the notes-transport decision: the plan's Goals bound only the contribution payload, and this widens where the sha goes. Owner: confirm it or narrow it before merge. Downstream consumer impact was checked: none of the actor readers (gates, critic_mode, critic_consolidate, evidence_notes, contribution, prawduct-hook) enumerates actor keys strictly. priors: none (prior_dispositions empty).", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-build-stamp.md", "plugin/lib/evidence.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "A git failure on a dev checkout is indistinguishable from a marketplace install", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. read_plugin_build discards run_git's stderr, so a timeout or git error on a real dev checkout records no build, and stats --by-build folds that fact into the same 'unstamped' row as marketplace installs and pre-field facts. An operator who sees unstamped rows on a dev build cannot tell which cause it was. This is acceptable for best-effort provenance and matches actor.branch's rule. If it ever matters, a debug-level trace of the reason would cover it. No edit is wanted for this merge.", "files": ["plugin/lib/evidence.py", "plugin/lib/stats.py"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: brookstalley/prawduct#1086 (telemetry: every 3.8 dev build records as 3.8.0-dev, so builds blur)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Both acceptance boxes are covered: stats --by-build splits a version by actor.build, and two tests pin that the contribution payload never carries build. The change record declares closes: [brookstalley/prawduct#1086]. Verify it, then call `/prawduct:backlog update 1086 status=shipped closed-by=scope:build-stamp` when the backlog skill's 'When to mark shipped' rule says.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/build-stamp.md"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "C-B3: open telemetry items next to the stats change were not assessed", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Two open items cover the stats surface this diff extends. #1058 (stats and contribute double-count ingested reviews): by_build inherits that double count, and because actor.build now travels through notes ingest, the same review can appear under the same build in two clones. #291 (window review-stats and flag zero-yield pruning candidates). No chunk updated either item. Assess them and update their status if this work changes them (`/prawduct:backlog`). Also checked: #1104 resolves as open and out of scope, as the plan says, and #1105 is a merged PR, not a dangling id.", "files": ["plugin/lib/stats.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check and Records Pass: no regressions, no oracle record clears a bar", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Read list (from learnings-files --for-diff): core.md, authoring.md, gates.md, hook-surface.md, release.md, tests.md. No finding reintroduces a pattern those rules warn against. The rule beginning 'Test subprocesses with HOME=tmp_path ... leak macOS Python's pyc cache' (tests.md) bears on the git-status dirty check. It is satisfied: __pycache__/ is ignored in this repo's .gitignore and in the test fixture, so bytecode does not mark a build +dirty. The rule beginning 'A persisted memo key must cover every input for the VALUE's lifetime' (gates.md) is satisfied: _build_memo is per-process and keyed by nothing, and its docstring says the running code cannot change under a running process. No learnings rules were added or changed this cycle. Records Pass covered the whole files_oracle set: api-contract.md, build-plan-build-stamp.md, data-model.md, kernel-v3-evidence-design.md and changes/build-stamp.md. None clears a bar: no shipped false claim, nothing misleads into action, no wrong command. The consumer note's 'Review, resolution and guard facts' understates the reach, since every append_fact kind is stamped, but it leads no reader into a wrong action, so it is not a finding. record_lint counts are all zero, with nothing unchecked.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/build-stamp.md"], "fid": "R-8"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 1, "note": 7}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": "build-stamp", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01", "02", "03"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02", "03"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": "eb4de60ea330e0d9cfc8e1a40665936e76b2d2ad", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-build-stamp.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/kernel-v3-evidence-design.md", ".prawduct/changes/build-stamp.md", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01", "02", "03"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-build-stamp.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-10-27T22:45:19Z"}}

